-- Proof sketch: Theorem 13.5 identifies the lower-semicontinuous hull of the positively
-- homogeneous convex function generated by `f` with the support function of the nonpositive
-- conjugate sublevel set. Theorem 14.2 then makes the recession cone of that hull polar to the
-- closed convex cone generated by `{xStar | f⋆ xStar ≤ 0}`. Using the hypotheses
-- `f 0 > 0 > inf f` together with the Chapter 7 closure-of-sublevel theorem, the recession cone
-- of that generated hull is exactly the closure of the generated cone
-- `{x | f x ≤ 0}`. The same argument for `f⋆` gives the reverse equality.

/-- Theorem 14.3: if `f` is a closed proper convex function on a finite-dimensional real
inner-product space, and hence in particular on `R^n`, with `f(0) > 0 > inf f`, then the polar
cone of the closed generated cone `((cone[ℝ] {x | f x ≤ 0}).closure : Set E)` is the closed
generated cone `((cone[ℝ] {xStar | f⋆ xStar ≤ 0}).closure : Set E)`. -/
theorem polarCone_closure_hull_nonpositiveSublevel_eq_closure_hull_nonpositiveSublevel_convexConjugate
    (f : E → WithBotTop ℝ) (hf : IsClosedProperConvex[ℝ] f)
    (hf_zero_pos : 0 < f 0) (hf_iInf_neg : (⨅ x : E, f x) < 0)
    : ((((cone[ℝ] {x : E | f x ≤ 0}).closure : Set E)ᵒ[ℝ] : PointedCone ℝ E) : Set E) =
        ((cone[ℝ] {xStar : E | f⋆ xStar ≤ 0}).closure : Set E) :=
  sorry

/-- Theorem 14.3: under the same hypotheses, the polar cone of the closed convex cone generated by
the nonpositive sublevel set `{xStar | f⋆ xStar ≤ 0}` is the closed generated cone
`((cone[ℝ] {x | f x ≤ 0}).closure : Set E)`. -/
theorem polarCone_closure_hull_nonpositiveSublevel_convexConjugate_eq_closure_hull_nonpositiveSublevel
    (f : E → WithBotTop ℝ) (hf : IsClosedProperConvex[ℝ] f)
    (hf_zero_pos : 0 < f 0) (hf_iInf_neg : (⨅ x : E, f x) < 0)
    : ((((cone[ℝ] {xStar : E | f⋆ xStar ≤ 0}).closure : Set E)ᵒ[ℝ] : PointedCone ℝ E) : Set E) =
        ((cone[ℝ] {x : E | f x ≤ 0}).closure : Set E) :=
  sorry

end
